      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:1:2:17:2",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) أَسْمَعُ الْحَدِيثَ مِنْكَ فَأَزِيدُ وَ أَنْقُصُ قَالَ إِنْ كُنْتَ تُرِيدُ مَعَانِيَهُ فَلَا بَأْسَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin yahya, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Ibr Azina, from Muhammad Bin Muslim who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘I hear the Hadeeth from you<sup>asws</sup>, so I (sometimes) increase and reduce.’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘If you had preserved its meaning, so there is no problem’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Husayn from ibn abu ‘Umayr from ibn ’Udhayna from Muhammad ibn Muslim who has said the following. “I asked abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.), ‘Can I add to or omit from a Hadith that I hear from you?’” He said, “It is alright, if you would preserve the meaning,’”"
        ]
      }
    },
